INT. ELEVATOR - NIGHT

A cramped steel box. Muzak. Floor numbers blinking: 14, 13, 12.

HECTOR (30s, wrinkled suit, a cake box balanced on one palm) leans in the corner, humming. BEA (30s, hospital badge, tote bag, a bouquet of sunflowers) stands near the doors, checking her phone.

Floor 11. The lights flicker. The elevator jerks to a halt.

HECTOR
Oh no.

BEA
No no no no.

Both lunge for the panel. Their hands collide on the emergency button. They freeze. Stare at each other.

HECTOR
Sorry.

BEA
You first.

HECTOR
No, you.

HECTOR
I'll push it.

^BEA
I'll push it.

They stop. He pulls his hand back. She presses the button. A buzzer rasps, and then silence.

HECTOR
(to himself)
Of course.

BEA
(to the ceiling)
Hello? Anyone?

Nothing. Hector sets the cake box on the floor and sits beside it. Bea sighs and sits too. He opens the lid and offers her a fork.
